<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert Steinberger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1840–1894</span> · Also known as Albert Barnes Steinberger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert Barnes Steinberger was an American adventurer who became premier of Samoa. Sent to the islands on a special mission by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> government in 1873, he returned in 1875 and drew up a constitution under which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malietoa-laupepa">Malietoa Laupepa</a> was king and he himself premier. In 1876 he was removed and deported on a British warship with the support of the British and American consuls.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-steinberger.jpg" alt="Albert Steinberger" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: New York Daily Graphic (newspaper), August 4, 1875, p. 254. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_Barnes_Steinberger.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
